00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hello everyone, today we will explain the usage of the setting layer tool.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,000
The setting layer tool is used to set the layer relationship between the panels.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The following is an example of a silver panel and a pure panel.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Describe the concept and principle of the setting layer tool.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
First, switch to the texture surface.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
You can see the front and back of the panel.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,000
This side is the front of the panel.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The slightly darker side is the back of the panel.

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The pure panel in our first project file is facing outwards.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
And the silver panel is facing outwards.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Let's use the setting layer tool first.

12
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Click on the silver panel, then click on the pure panel.

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Open the simulation.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The silver panel is simulated outside the pure panel.

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
At this time, the middle arrow is the plus sign.

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
If we click on the change to the minus sign, open the simulation.

17
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
You can see that the silver panel is simulated inside the pure panel.

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
In summary, if the middle arrow is the plus sign,

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000
then the selected panel will be simulated outside the selected panel.

20
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
If it is the minus sign, it is the opposite.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Let's open the second project file.

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
At this time, the silver panel is facing outwards.

23
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
The pure panel is also facing outwards.

24
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
We use the setting layer tool to click on the silver panel first.

25
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Then click on the pure panel.

26
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Open the simulation.

27
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
You can see that the silver panel is simulated again outside the front of the pure panel.

28
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
This is because the setting layer tool is simulated on the panel layer,

29
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
and the second simulation is affected by the opposite side of the selected panel.

30
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
We can see the selected panel as moving,

31
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
and the selected panel is fixed.

32
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,000
If the middle arrow is the plus sign,

33
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
then the selected panel will always be simulated outside the front of the selected panel.

34
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
If it is the minus sign, it is the opposite.

35
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Next, let's take this jacket as an example.

36
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
When we make 3D clothing,

37
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
the front of the panel is usually facing outwards,

38
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
and the back of the panel is facing outwards.

39
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
When the fabric is of the opposite material,

40
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:58,000
the effect is the same,

41
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
and when the thick texture surface is opened,

42
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
the display effect of the clothing is not affected.

43
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
But this clothing uses a fabric with a clear difference in the opposite side.

44
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Its side should face outwards.

45
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
In addition, in order to simulate a stable wearing effect,

46
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:19,000
we will use the setting layer tool to set the layer relationship between the large panel and the side.

47
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Then we will point the large panel to the side,

48
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
and simulate the outside of the side.

49
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
In this case,

50
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
if we turn the side over,

51
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
then the large panel will be the same as what we talked about in the previous demonstration.

52
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Simulate the outside of the side panel.

53
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
So we need to use the setting layer tool,

54
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
click on the symbol in the arrow,

55
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
you can see that the plus sign has become the minus sign.

56
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Open the simulation again,

57
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,000
then the large panel will simulate the outside of the side panel,

58
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
which is the display effect we want to get in the end.

